('use_of_english_0300', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "An ''audition'' is a tryout for a role, unrelated to the ending of a play.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Criticism'' is commentary about the play, not the opposite of its ending.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "A ''climax'' is the peak of tension, close to but not the same as the final resolution -- and not its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option opposite in meaning to the underlined word(s).

The dramatist provided a satisfactory

denouement

to the play?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "audition", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "criticism", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "introduction", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "climax", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', '''Denouement'' means the final resolution/ending of a play; its opposite is ''introduction'' (the beginning).', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0301', 'Use of English', 'Consonants', 'Consonant Sounds', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "3p5hul"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Father'' has the voiced /ð/ sound, not voiceless /θ/.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''They'' has the voiced /ð/ sound.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''That'' also has the voiced /ð/ sound.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that has the same consonant sound as the one represented by the letters underlined.

Heal

th

y?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "father", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "path", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "they", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "that", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'The ''th'' in ''healthy'' is the voiceless /θ/ sound (as in ''thin''). ''Path'' also has voiceless /θ/, while ''father'', ''they'', and ''that'' all have the voiced /ð/.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0302', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "B", "explanation": "''Imperative'' means urgent or commanding, an unrelated quality.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Subjective'' is essentially a synonym of opinionated (biased by personal views), not its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Discursive'' means rambling or wide-ranging in discussion, not the opposite of being opinionated.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option opposite in meaning to the underlined word(s).

