person?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "an objective", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "B", "text": "an imperative", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "a subjective", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "a discursive", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'A', '''Opinionated'' means stubbornly attached to one''s own views; its opposite is ''objective'' (open-minded, unbiased).', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0303', 'Use of English', 'Stress', 'Word Stress', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "stfgmb"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Downgrading'' as a continuous verb form is naturally stressed on ''grad'' (down-GRAD-ing), a different pattern.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Prescribing'' is stressed on its second syllable (pre-SCRIB-ing), not the first.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Internal'' is stressed on its second syllable (in-TER-nal), not the first.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that has the same stress pattern as the given word.

downtrodden?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "downgrading", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "prescribing", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "functional", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "internal", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', '''Downtrodden'' is stressed on its first syllable (DOWN-trod-den), a strong-weak-weak pattern. ''Functional'' (FUNC-tion-al) shares this exact pattern.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0304', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Vivid'' means vibrant or bright, an unrelated quality.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Cruel'' is a different negative quality, not the opposite of invidious.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Difficult'' is close in feeling to invidious (a hard task) rather than its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option opposite in meaning to the underlined word(s).

The officer was given an

invidious

task?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "vivid", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "cruel", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "pleasant", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "difficult", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', '''Invidious'' describes something unpleasant or likely to cause resentment; its opposite is ''pleasant''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0305', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Antonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "v4agon"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'medium', 'none', '[{"option": "B", "explanation": "Being ''represented by a counsel'' is itself a form of appearing by proxy, not its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Not appear at all'' is a different scenario entirely, not the direct opposite of appearing via a representative.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "Answering by phone is still a form of remote (proxy-like) participation, not its opposite.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option

opposite in meaning

to the underlined word or phrase.

