('use_of_english_0307', 'Use of English', 'Stress', 'Word Stress', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "stfgmb"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Reform'' is stressed on its second syllable (re-FORM).", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Intact'' is stressed on its second syllable (in-TACT).", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Obscure'' is stressed on its second syllable (ob-SCURE).", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that has the same stress pattern as the given word.

Refuse (noun)', '[{"label": "A", "text": "reform", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "intact", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "obscure", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "phantom", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Refuse'' as a noun is stressed on the first syllable (REF-use). ''Phantom'' (PHAN-tom) shares this first-syllable stress pattern.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0308', 'Use of English', 'Idiomatic expressions', 'Figures of Speech', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "lwt4xp"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "This is the opposite meaning -- ''made a pile'' means gained money, not lost it.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Broke even'' means neither gained nor lost money, a different outcome from ''making a pile''.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Cut corners'' means to take shortcuts, an unrelated idiom about method rather than profit.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option nearest in meaning to the underlined word(s).

