('use_of_english_0309', 'Use of English', 'Grammatical usage', 'Gerunds after Prepositions', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "e1a7oj"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Sell'' is a bare infinitive, but ''with a view to'' requires a gerund, not a bare infinitive.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Have sold'' is a perfect infinitive form, which doesn''t fit after the fixed phrase ''with a view to''.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Be selling'' is not the required gerund form after ''to'' in this fixed phrase.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

The man is refurbishing the flat with a view to ......it?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "sell", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "selling", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "have sold", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "be selling", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', '''With a view to'' is a fixed phrase always followed by a gerund (''-ing'' form), not a bare infinitive: ''with a view to selling it''.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0310', 'Use of English', 'Vocabulary', 'Contextual Word Pairs', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "nvgfyg"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Understanding'' doesn''t capture the specific respect/submission that African custom expects toward elders.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "''Indifference'' (not caring) contradicts the idea of showing something positive to elders.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''Satisfaction'' is unrelated to the respectful attitude expected toward elders.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the option that best completes the gap(S).

It is African for a younger person to show ...... to elders?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "understanding", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "indifference", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "deference", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "satisfaction", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'C', '''Deference'' means respectful submission to someone''s wishes or authority, exactly what a younger person is expected to show elders.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0311', 'Use of English', 'Synonyms/antonyms', 'Synonyms', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "r0mfcp"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'recall', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "''Instability'' refers to lack of stability generally, not specifically material lack.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "''Difficulty'' is too generic and doesn''t specifically mean material deprivation.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}, {"option": "D", "explanation": "''The slums'' describes a place associated with poverty, not the word''s actual meaning.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Choose the

