.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "instability", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "want", "isCorrect": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "difficulty", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "the slums", "isCorrect": false}]'::jsonb, 'B', '''Poverty'' means lack of basic necessities; ''want'' is the classic literary synonym for this state of need.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
('use_of_english_0312', 'Use of English', 'Vocabulary and expressions in context', 'Sentence Interpretation (Idiom)', NULL, '[{"weight": 1, "conceptId": "fno6b9"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 2, 'application', 60, 'low', 'none', '[{"option": "A", "explanation": "This only restates the beginning, ignoring what the sentence says about the ending.", "misconceptionId": "confused_similar_concepts"}, {"option": "B", "explanation": "This wrongly projects into the future (''will not end''), while the sentence describes something that already happened.", "misconceptionId": "misunderstood_terminology"}, {"option": "C", "explanation": "Hedging with ''almost'' softens the sentence''s direct claim that the crisis simply ended suddenly.", "misconceptionId": "overgeneralized_rule"}]'::jsonb, '{}', 'jamb_past_question', 2005, 'JAMB', '{}', 'Select the option that best explains the information conveyed in the sentence.

The crisis ended as suddenly as it began?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "The crisis had suddenly begun", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "The crisis will not end suddenly", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "The crisis stopped almost immediately", "isCorrect": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "The crisis stopped immediately", "isCorrect": true}]'::jsonb, 'D', '''Ended as suddenly as it began'' emphasizes the crisis stopped abruptly and without warning; ''stopped immediately'' captures this directly.', 'live', '{"totalAttempts": 0, "correctCount": 0, "avgResponseTimeMs": 0, "distractorSelectionCounts": {}}'::jsonb),
